  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C2.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet, C1 (the input decoupling capacitor on the Display_Power_Switch rail, in parallel with C2) is drawn with value '0.1uF/16V'.",
      "expected": "The specification's component-matching table explicitly assigns C1 to the PDI 'C2 default' group of 1 µF/25 V capacitors (C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V). A 0.1 µF/16 V part is neither the stated value nor the stated voltage rating.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 0.1uF/16V  (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, page 5, left of the boost converter, between Display_Power_Switch and GND)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD power-switch/boost-input rail loses the 1 µF bulk decoupling the reference design specifies (only 0.1 µF remains, plus C2), and the 16 V rating is below the 25 V the reference calls for. This is a deviation from the intended PDI G1-group implementation; behaviour impact is minor (slightly poorer transient filtering on the display rail) but it is a clear value/rating mismatch against the spec.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the build matches the specification (FAN53610 topology and EN/MODE/FB wiring, barrel-jack battery-disconnect, Q2 high-side switch with R2 pull-up, EPD part numbers and G1 values, reset switch, UART header). The one deviation I can evidence is C1, drawn as 0.1 µF/16 V on the Display_Power_Switch rail whereas the spec lists C1 among the 1 µF/25 V group, so I report it as a wrong-value/wrong-rating anomaly with moderate confidence."
}

